  "question": {
    "text": "A lens having refractive index 1.6 has focal length of 12 cm , when it is in air. Find the focal length of the lens when it is placed in water.<br/>(Take refractive index of water as 1.28)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "98Cm5",
      "text": "355 mm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZeXBf",
      "text": "288 mm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Q24NO",
      "text": "555 mm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1Od3W",
      "text": "655 mm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As we know,<br/>$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=\\left[\\frac{\\mu_{\\mathrm{L}}}{\\mu_{\\mathrm{m}}}-1\\right]\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right]$<br/>For air $\\mu_{\\mathrm{m}}=1$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1}{12}=[1.6-1]\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right] \\\\ & \\frac{1}{12}=\\frac{6}{10}\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right] \\\\ & {\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right]=\\frac{10}{72}}\\end{aligned}$<br/>For water<br/>$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=\\left[\\frac{1.6}{1.28}-1\\right]\\left[\\frac{10}{72}\\right]=\\frac{32}{128} \\times \\frac{10}{72}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{10}{72} \\\\ & \\mathrm{f}=28.8 \\mathrm{~cm} \\\\ & \\mathrm{f}=288 \\mathrm{~mm}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
